---
import SiteShell from '../layouts/SiteShell.astro';
import { fetchArtist, type Artist } from '../lib/lastfm';

let artist: Artist | null = null;
try {
  artist = await fetchArtist();
} catch (err) {
  console.warn(`[lastfm] ${err}, keeping the fallback artist`);
}
---

<SiteShell>
  <h2>Welcome to my website</h2>
  <p>
    You may be thinking to yourself, "Oliver, your website looks a little crazy." I know right. It's an homage to the
    early internet and GeoCities era of personal site dev and it has been a ton of fun to work on.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you don't know me, you can probably guess my name :^) I'm a CS student at UW-Madison though I was born and raised
    in Seattle. You can learn more about me at <a href="/webmaster/">webmaster</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of my free time goes into hanging with friends and building things. Some recent ones: a Tauri desktop app for
    mapping out social graphs in Neo4j, and a Go bot that watches company career pages so I don't have to. This site
    renovation (renovation #4 actually) is the latest project. It's not done. It may never be done. That's kind of the
    point.
  </p>
  <p>
    Off the computer it's reading, fishing, and listening to music (Recently{' '}
    <a
      class="lastfm-artist"
      href="https://www.last.fm/user/oliverohrt"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      title={artist?.title}
    >
      {artist?.name ?? 'Earl Sweatshirt'}
    </a>
    ). Right now I'm studying abroad in Thailand, so expect blog posts about that when the blog exists.
  </p>
  <p>
    Thanks for stopping by. <a href="/guestbook/">Sign the guestbook</a> on your way out.
  </p>
</SiteShell>
